# Presence of this file makes npm pack/publish use ONLY the package.json
# `files` whitelist — the neighboring .gitignore (which ignores the
# prepare-generated `skill/`) is not consulted for packing.
# The real risk this guards is `prepare` never running (e.g. npm config
# ignore-scripts=true): then skill/ is absent and the tarball loses the
# bundled skill. The release workflow stages the skill explicitly and
# asserts `skill/SKILL.md` is in the packed tarball before npm publish, so
# publishing does not depend on lifecycle scripts at all.
